/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:3119:Log entries are append-only. Annotation and correction never modify the original entry. They create a new Log entry with `event_type` set to `log_annotation_added` or `log_correction_added`, and with `annotation_of` or `correction_of` pointing to the original `log_entry_id`.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:3185:Support friction on `task_completed`, `task_failed`, and Task-specific deviations recorded with `plan_realized`; no new deviation event type is introduced. Other event types retain ordinary notes. The friction object may be supplied when the event is admitted, or later through `log_annotation_added` with `annotation_of` pointing to that outcome/deviation entry. Reject invalid or oversized notes without silent truncation. Each note inherits the shared envelope's actor, Device, effective/recorded times and provenance. Model explanations remain labelled advisory candidates until accepted; acceptance retains their inferred/model provenance and establishes no proven cause. Omission means no explanation supplied, not friction-free execution.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:3187:Replacing or withdrawing a note appends `log_correction_added`, with `correction_of` pointing to the entry containing the superseded note and the correction explicitly scoped to its friction assertion. Originals remain unchanged; correcting friction alone cannot change completion or duration claims. On a friction-only correction, `event_payload.friction` is the replacement object or `null` for withdrawal. Review and future learning follow admitted correction links, expose unresolved competing corrections, and retain distinct attributed notes rather than selecting by latest timestamp.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:3193:**Review and learning boundary.** The Log review report shows the Task/outcome ref, original planned baseline and actual duration with their evidence/coverage, absolute and relative difference when comparable, current attributed notes and correction status, and permitted linked decisions. Offer add/correct note, inspect evidence/decision, or propose a separate Task-estimate/model correction; skipping requires no explanation. Notes, refs, reports and derived model inputs obey current source/Compartment disclosure and retention policy; denied context is never copied into a note or summary.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:3195:Phase 2 captures explanatory review evidence; Bayesian updating remains post-MVP under `UBU-Q0116`. A note is neither a measurement correction nor a duration override: never infer minutes to subtract from text, automatically discard/down-weight an observation, or change distribution parameters merely because friction is present. Numeric errors require separately admitted corrections to duration evidence. Future learning consumes the corrected outcome/duration evidence with its linked current notes and provenance, counting each completion once regardless of annotation count. Failed/partial attempts and deviations are not completed-duration draws; any censored-data, grouping, covariate or outlier policy remains for `UBU-Q0116`. Missing notes establish no cause or normality. Learned `(min_seconds, mode_seconds, p95_seconds)` suggestions require explicit user review and ordinary validated admission before affecting Plans; the kernel continues to receive only admitted duration models.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:3255:**Contradiction, correction and revocation.** Material conflicting evidence, corrected/revoked claims or changed use/versions invalidate the applicable assessment before affected Plan reuse, projection or execution. Append `log_correction_added` and separately admitted replacement Snapshot/mutations where supported, retaining the original claim and why its interpretation changed. Recalculate affected Plans from the corrected admitted view. A later legitimate state change need not negate a supported historical effect at an earlier time; reassess current-state freshness separately.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:3523:Realtime models are replaceable interaction backends for the primary MVP camera-and-voice surface (`UBU-D0292`), including conversation, capture, triage and short-horizon repair. UbU represents a realtime run as a lightweight `RealtimeInteractionSession`, not as a Task, Calendar event, canonical Log entry, or raw sensor stream. A session records the consented interaction context and source boundary; the model's outputs are `RealtimeCandidateUpdate` records until admitted through the ordinary planner, Log, Snapshot, Compartment, and review rules.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:4456:After invocation, UbU should create or update a context exposure summary. The summary records the actual provider/model/tool used, invocation refs, source counts and categories, Compartments, Identities, Associations, and Relationships exposed, raw-versus-summary/reference volume, redactions and exclusions, retention/training profile, prompt-injection exposure notes, approval and routing Log refs, downstream candidate refs, and any denied or omitted context that affected output quality. The summary is a review artifact and must not contain secrets or unnecessary raw payload.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:4722:The Phase 1 cockpit seed is the already frozen §4.1.2 loop: one Task with title, Objective, duration/work window, status and provenance; a compact why-now explanation covering timing, dependency/blocker, affect/staleness and top risk/opportunity; visible worker/projection state where relevant; and one-action access to the full Plan, considered alternatives/constraints and permitted evidence. Explain what each control records, distinguish recommendation from commitment and predicted effects from observed outcomes, and expose the existing review/correction and projection-preview paths. Label fixture/mock behavior explicitly.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:4880:**Transient excerpt review.** Fetch a bounded excerpt from the currently authorized pinned source through a purpose/actor/Device-bound finite view lease. Display it as temporary source text with permitted provenance and an expiry indicator. A raw preview requires source/read authority and `review` permission, and does not imply retention, downstream-use or export permission. Do not embed preview text in durable findings, Task descriptions, Logs, saved prompts, search indexes, telemetry, autosave, backups or default clipboard content. A copy/save/export request is a separately checked operation under the corresponding policies.
/home/sean/ubu-design/DESIGN.md:5727:The canonical instance may hold a local GitHub credential only when it is itself the writer for a human-approved local projection. It does not need to see worker-held tokens and must not store raw GitHub secrets in Objectives, Tasks, ContextBundles, Logs, run artifacts, projection payloads, or External References.

